# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — NEVER commit.
#
# `.env*` rather than a bare `.env`, so a stray `.env.local`, `.env.bak` or
# `.env.old` can't slip through; `.env.example` is negated back in because it
# is the template and holds only placeholders.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scraped content and run state. All of it is regenerated by `extract`, all of
# it is per-operator, and cache/ alone runs to several GB.
#
# Note the `dir/*` + negation form throughout. `data/` alone would exclude the
# DIRECTORY, and git cannot re-include a file inside an excluded directory —
# `!data/.gitkeep` would then silently do nothing. The app creates these dirs
# on demand, but a fresh clone gets them from the .gitkeep files.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
cache/*
!cache/.gitkeep
state/*
!state/.gitkeep
logs/*
!logs/.gitkeep

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test fixtures: the real Baseball-Reference pages only.
#
# Those are ~3.4 MB of verbatim Sports Reference HTML, and their terms of use
# restrict redistribution — so they stay local and `tests/refresh_fixtures.py`
# rebuilds them from cache/ (or, failing that, from the network). Everything
# else in tests/fixtures/ is ours and is committed: the hand-reviewed golden
# JSON, and the two hand-written title_*.html files that stand in for a page
# whose original could not be re-fetched. See README.md § Testing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tests/fixtures/*.html
!tests/fixtures/title_*.html
!tests/fixtures/.gitkeep

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
#
# .venv/ is per-machine: every clone builds its own from requirements.txt.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS
#
# .vscode/ and sports-data-gen.code-workspace are deliberately NOT ignored —
# they contain no absolute paths (every one goes through ${workspaceFolder}),
# they wire a clone to its own venv, and README.md § VS Code documents them as
# intentional.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.tmp
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
